// Public Objective-C interface names imported by Foundation/Foundation.h.
// Reviewed against Apple's macOS 15.5 SDK public headers, not implementations.
// Define both X-macros before including; this file deliberately has no guard.
//
// COMMON: 203 interfaces visible under macOS, iOS-device and iOS-simulator
// header conditionals, excluding types unavailable on macOS. They retain all
// 28 names in the original declaration allowlist. PLATFORM: 71 other imported
// interfaces; these contribute to name-conflict detection, not the common
// superclass allowlist. The union has 274 distinct names.
//
// Validation: Apple Clang, Objective-C with ARC/modules disabled, an empty
// subclass of every COMMON name; macOS 15.5 (arm64/x86_64), iOS 18.5 header
// targets (arm64 device; arm64/x86_64 simulator). iOS checks use cross-platform
// declarations in the same macOS SDK, not a standalone iOS SDK or runtime.
// PLATFORM names were checked under their available header targets. These
// are reviewed SDK declaration surfaces, not availability on every SDK,
// deployment version, Apple platform, or ARC mode. No ivar layout, native
// method body, subclass behavior, or source equivalence is implied.
//
// Forward declarations, protocols and non-Foundation OS object types are
// excluded. Add names only with public interface and availability evidence.

